# POST /sop/check: an SOP and the lines of one run in; every step in order, or the first that fails, out
route     POST /sop/check
handler   sop_check
memo      the contract of POST /sop/check on tiesapi.com
input
  {"federated_id", "sop": "<the SOP text>", "lines": ["<step 0 line>", "<step 1 line>", ...], "receipts": [{issued_at, receipt}, ...]}
  the SOP's steps are its lines "<k> sha256:<64 hex>", k = 1..N; receipts are optional, one per line, from POST /receipt
processing
  1 the body is one JSON object of at most 65,536 characters, and federated_id has its form
  2 the SOP's id is the sha256 of its exact text; read steps 1..N
  3 each line passes every rule of POST /receipt
  4 line k is step k: label = step k of the SOP (step 0: the SOP itself), parents include line k-1,
    prev_nonce = the nonce of line k-1, and sha256 of the nonce = prev_nonce
  5 with receipts: each verifies, and issued_at never goes backwards
output
  200 {valid, complete, sop, steps, done, timed, error}: valid only when steps 0..N are all there, in order
  400 only for a malformed body or federated_id; a run that fails is 200 with valid: false and the first failure in error
  check: skip, repeat or reorder one step and valid is false
graph
  builds on receipt
  builds on verify
